WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.290
In Iceland, at Krafla, rifting opened
the ground by about 7 metres between 1975

2
00:00:06.340 --> 00:00:08.470
and 1984.

3
00:00:08.520 --> 00:00:12.610
In South America, the land is
being lifted to build the Andes.

4
00:00:12.660 --> 00:00:18.870
And in California, the San Andreas
fault zone runs about 1,300 kilometres.

5
00:00:18.920 --> 00:00:22.290
One planet, three very different places.

6
00:00:22.340 --> 00:00:24.690
So what happens where plates meet?

7
00:00:24.740 --> 00:00:29.690
In this mission, you'll see how stretching
crust can drop a valley between faults,

8
00:00:29.740 --> 00:00:32.150
from East Africa to the Red Sea.

9
00:00:32.200 --> 00:00:35.590
Then you'll map where the world's
biggest earthquakes cluster,

10
00:00:35.640 --> 00:00:38.950
about 81 per cent of
them around the Pacific.

11
00:00:39.000 --> 00:00:42.530
Your mission: find out what
happens where plates meet.
